            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-accordion" id="faq-accordion">
            <!-- Question 1 -->
            <div class="faq-item active">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-ans-1" id="faq-q-1">
                <span class="faq-q-icon">01</span>
                <span class="faq-q-text">Who is eligible to participate in Xavathon 2027?</span>
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
                </span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-ans-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-1">
                <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                  <p>
                    <strong>Xavathon is open to everyone!</strong> Students, faculty members, administrative staff, and alumni of <strong>St. Xavier’s College (Autonomous), Kolkata</strong> run alongside collegiate athletes from across West Bengal, running clubs, and passionate amateur or competitive marathoners nationwide.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    There are separate distance categories designed for all fitness levels, ranging from beginner leisure walkers to seasoned distance racers.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Question 2 -->
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-ans-2" id="faq-q-2">
                <span class="faq-q-icon">02</span>
                <span class="faq-q-text">What are the race categories, routes, and timing cut-offs?</span>
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
                </span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-ans-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-2">
                <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                  <ul class="faq-list-bullets">
                    <li><strong>3 KM Fun Run:</strong> Open to all age groups. An untimed spirited run and walk with <em>no cut-off time</em>. Ideal for first-timers, friends, and families.</li>
                    <li><strong>5 KM Challenge Run:</strong> Professionally timed via electronic RFID bib. Cut-off time: <strong>60 minutes</strong>. Perfect for personal fitness milestones.</li>
                    <li><strong>10 KM Championship Run:</strong> Competitive championship course timed via RFID splits. Cut-off time: <strong>100 minutes</strong>. Podium cash rewards and trophies for top finishers in Men’s and Women’s divisions.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Question 3 -->
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-ans-3" id="faq-q-3">
                <span class="faq-q-icon">03</span>
                <span class="faq-q-text">What does the theme "Towards Greener Footprints" mean?</span>
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
                </span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-ans-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-3">
                <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                  <p>
                    Xavathon’s core philosophy is sustainability. We implement a strict <strong>Zero-Plastic Policy</strong> across all water stations and college grounds using compostable bagasse cups.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    For every single runner registered, St. Xavier's College commits to planting a native tree sapling during monsoon afforestation drives. Additionally, our finisher medals are cast from plantable seed paper or recycled metals, and event bibs are printed on mineral paper.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Question 4 -->
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-ans-4" id="faq-q-4">
                <span class="faq-q-icon">04</span>
                <span class="faq-q-text">What is included in the Official Runner's Race Kit?</span>
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
                </span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-ans-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-4">
                <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                  <p>Every confirmed participant receives a complete athlete kit containing:</p>
                  <ul class="faq-list-bullets">
                    <li>Official Xavathon breathable dry-fit athletic running jersey</li>
                    <li>Electronic RFID timing bib (for 5K & 10K categories)</li>
                    <li>Eco-friendly organic cotton tote sling bag</li>
                    <li>Finisher Medal awarded immediately upon crossing the finish line</li>
                    <li>Post-race hot wholesome breakfast & electrolyte refreshments</li>
                    <li>Official digital Finisher E-Certificate with verified split times</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Question 5 -->
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-ans-5" id="faq-q-5">
                <span class="faq-q-icon">05</span>
                <span class="faq-q-text">Where is the Race Village, Start Line, and Assembly Point?</span>
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
                </span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-ans-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-5">
                <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                  <p>
                    The Race Village, flag-off line, and celebratory finish line are located at the historic <strong>St. Xavier’s College Main Campus, 30 Mother Teresa Sarani (Park Street), Kolkata</strong>.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    Gates open at <strong>4:45 AM</strong>. Official flag-off sequence:
                    <br />&bull; <strong>10 KM Championship:</strong> 5:45 AM
                    <br />&bull; <strong>5 KM Challenge:</strong> 6:00 AM
                    <br />&bull; <strong>3 KM Fun Run:</strong> 6:15 AM
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Question 6 -->
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-ans-6" id="faq-q-6">
                <span class="faq-q-icon">06</span>
                <span class="faq-q-text">Will there be medical support, baggage storage, and hydration stations?</span>
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
                </span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-ans-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-6">
                <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                  <p>
                    <strong>Yes, full safety infrastructure is deployed.</strong> Hydration stations are positioned at every 1.5 km offering clean water, electrolytes, and glucose.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    Mobile medical squads with certified paramedics and on-standby BLS ambulances will cover the route. Secure, supervised baggage counters will be available inside campus, as well as a physiotherapy stretch-and-recovery lounge at the finish line.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Question 7 -->
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-ans-7" id="faq-q-7">
                <span class="faq-q-icon">07</span>
                <span class="faq-q-text">How and when can I collect my Bib and Race Kit?</span>
                <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg>
                </span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer" id="faq-ans-7" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-q-7">
                <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                  <p>
                    Bib collection takes place at the <strong>Xavathon Expo</strong> hosted in the College Auditorium 2 days prior to race day from <strong>10:00 AM to 6:00 PM</strong>.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    Please carry your registration confirmation email (digital or printed) and a valid photo ID. Outstation participants unable to collect beforehand can avail early-morning bib distribution starting at 4:45 AM on race day.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
